              "explanation": "Recovery Block Scheme If the result is rejected, another alternative program is then executed. The program will be repeated until an acceptable result is generated by one of the n alternatives or until all the alternative programs fail. The probability of failure of the RB scheme, $P_{rb}$, is as follows:\n[Tex]$$ P_{rb}= \\prod_{i=1}^n (e_i+t_{2i})+\\sum_{i=1}^n t_{1i}e_i\\left ( \\prod_{j=1}^{i-1} (e_j+t_{2j}) \\right) $$ [/Tex] where [Tex]$e_i$ [/Tex] = probability of failure for version Pi\n[Tex]$t_{1i}$ [/Tex] = probability that acceptance test I judges an incorrect result as correct t [Tex]$t_{2i}$ [/Tex] = probability that acceptance test I judge a correct result as incorrect. The above equation corresponds to the case when all versions fail the acceptance test. The second term corresponds to the probability that acceptance test I judges an incorrect result as correct at the ith trial of the n versions."
