              "explanation": "This is the ratio of the number of operator occurrences to the number of operand occurrences in the program, i.e., L = n1/n2 where n1 is the number of operator occurrences and n2 is the number of operand occurrences.\nProgram difficulty (D): This is the ratio of the number of unique operators to the total number of operators in the program, i.e., D = (n1/2) * (N2/n2)\nProgram effort (E): This is the product of program volume (V) and program difficulty (D), i.e., E = V*D"
